<item><title>Bank of Ghana cuts policy rate to 11% as banks expect cheaper loans</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gh/bank-of-ghana-cuts-policy-rate-to-11-as-banks-expect-0ad81b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gh/bank-of-ghana-cuts-policy-rate-to-11-as-banks-expect-0ad81b/</guid><category>Ghana</category><description>The 300-basis-point cut follows a Monetary Policy Committee meeting, and the Ghana Association of Banks says lending rates are set to fall in the coming months.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:34:08 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gh/bank-of-ghana-cuts-policy-rate-to-11-as-banks-expect-0ad81b/share.jpg" length="42898" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gh/bank-of-ghana-cuts-policy-rate-to-11-as-banks-expect-0ad81b/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
